{"name":"Adobe Glow","hex":"#c99f93","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"adobe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An unburnt brick dried in the sun.","The earth from which such bricks are made."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adobe"},{"term":"glow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To emit heat and light without a flame.","To emit heat and light without a flame."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of heat and light being emitted by a hot object.","A state of heat being emitted by a person or an animal's body."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Adobe","blocks":[{"text":"Adobe is a building material made from loam and organic materials. Adobe is Spanish for mudbrick. In some English-speaking regions of Spanish heritage, such as the Southwestern United States, the term is used to refer to any kind of earthen construction, or various architectural styles like Pueblo Revival or Territorial Revival. Most adobe buildings are similar in appearance to cob and rammed earth buildings. Adobe is among the earliest building materials, and is used throughout the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg/330px-Adobe_wall_%28detail%29_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe","wikidata":"Q183496"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg/500px-AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg/500px-AdobeSurfaceCoatingRenewalOnWall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Renewal of the surface coating of an adobe wall in Chamisal, New Mexico","link":"https://